 ### 7.6 Calls and the media plane
 
+Response builders retain every Via header in request order (RFC 3261
+8.2.6.2), including both SDP and bodyless responses. `tests/Messages` pins
+multi-proxy responses. The optional bounded `TRACE_CALL_SIP` diagnostic
+is documented in the README; it adds metadata only and leaves the bus ABI
+unchanged.
+
+An offerless incoming re-INVITE sends the existing SDP as an offer in its
+200 response and awaits a matching-CSeq ACK answer, bounded to 32 seconds.
+The cached response is reused for duplicate INVITEs without extending the
+deadline; stale ACKs cannot consume a pending offer. A bodyless UPDATE stays
+bodyless. Only the existing media leg is supported: changed offers get 488,
+and an unsupported or missing ACK answer ends the dialog with BYE. Complete
+transaction timers and timed 2xx retransmission remain outside this change.
+The local active signal precedes the initial ACK, so never use it alone as
+proof of remote answer or working audio.
+
