+### Incoming in-dialog offer/answer
+
+An offerless re-INVITE on an accepted incoming call receives the current
+session SDP as an offer in the 200 response. Its matching-CSeq ACK must
+contain a compatible answer. Old ACKs cannot complete a newer exchange;
+repeated INVITEs receive the cached response without extending the 32-second
+ACK deadline. A missing or unsupported ACK answer ends the dialog with BYE.
+A bodyless UPDATE remains bodyless.
+
+This path deliberately retains the existing media endpoint, codec, payload,
+octet alignment and DTMF parameters. Unsupported offered changes receive 488;
+media redirection, hold/transfer, a complete SIP transaction layer and timed
+2xx retransmission are not implemented. Local `active` still precedes the
+initial ACK and is not proof of remote answer or two-way audio.
+
+Validated with unit cases and isolated TCP/UDP peers, then incoming calls on
+an LG V30 US998 / China Unicom, including a roughly 60-second call after a
+normal default-system boot with human confirmation of clear two-way speech.
+No raw subscriber traces are included in this contribution.
+
